{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' answer/final_closeout_summary.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Final Closeout Summary\n\nThe correct award cap for this closeout is `$1,600.00` from `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. That document controls because it is the newest dated award document and expressly supersedes the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`.\n\nThe corrected reimbursable total is `$1,588.00`, leaving `$12.00` remaining under the cap.\n\nUseful prior work was preserved where it still matched the current evidence: approval of `G-001` for garden supplies, approval of `G-003` for accessibility printing, rejection of `G-004` for staff gifts, and the previously captured outcome facts about seedling kits and Braille flyers.\n\nWrong prior work was corrected where the draft relied on stale or incomplete information: the cap was reduced from the superseded `$2,000.00` figure to `$1,600.00`, `G-002` was reduced to the `$120.00` volunteer-refreshments cap, `G-005` was changed from approved to rejected under the current eligibility and receipt rules, and omitted expense `G-006` was added as an approved `$68.00` postage charge.\n\nOutcome facts from `05_outcomes.md` to retain in the packet:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
